A.  Smears show abundant blood with scattered variably sized pieces of follicular epithelium, mainly caught up within pieces of blood clot.  These are mostly loosely cohesive and they are composed of cells with uniform round nuclei.  Some of the 
fragments are sheet-like and some of the fragments show follicular structures.  The thin preparation shows lysed blood and histiocytes.  The cell block preparation shows similar findings.

