pathology_extended:
Malignant cells present; 
     Papillary thyroid carcinoma. 
Per requisition: "Left thyroid nodule".

Findings consistent with colloid nodule; 
No malignant cells seen; 
Sample showing ample cellularity. 
The smears show numerous fragments of follicular epithelium; over 50 are counted on the smears.  The fragments tend to be quite large and the epithelium appears sheet like.  The cells are small and bland.  A small amount of colloid is seen and there are 
scattered pigmented histiocytes.  The thin preparation shows additional fragments.  These tend to be smaller, but the cells are bland.  There are no microacinar structures noted.  The cell block preparation and clot preparation show numerous pieces of 
follicular epithelium with epithelial strips appearing quite large indicating the presence of large follicles.

pathology_diagnosis:
Consistent with colloid nodule or dominant nodule of goiter; 
No malignant cells seen. 
B.  Shows adequate cellularity.  Follicular cells are mainly in loosely cohesive variably sized fragments.  The cells show round uniform nuclei.  The thin prep shows abundant colloid, histiocytes, and rare benign-appearing epithelial fragments.

